@startuml i4-backup-restore
' I4 S2 / E26 — backup and restore (docs/hld/71-i4-wave4.md §71.3, D33), and the S5 / E29 purge
' guard (§71.6, ТЗ ¶216). The backup service runs on the already-local postgres:16 image.

title Daily backup, restore, and the purge that needs a fresh backup

skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 6
skinparam BoxPadding 8

actor "administrator\n(shell)" as OP
actor "ADMIN\n(web)" as A

box "docker compose" #F3FFF3
  participant "backup service\n(postgres:16 loop)" as BK
  database "postgres" as PG
  collections "recordings-data\nvolume" as REC
  collections "./backups/\n*.dump, *.tar.gz,\nlast.json" as DIR
  participant "backend\n(reads last.json)" as BE
end box

== 1. Daily loop (and make backup-now) ==
loop every 24 h
  BK -> PG : pg_dump -Fc (compressed, ¶390)
  BK -> REC : tar.gz of the recordings
  BK -> DIR : write dump + archive
  BK -> DIR : rotate: keep SIM_BACKUP_KEEP (default 14)
  BK -> DIR : last.json {ts, sizes, sha256, status}
end

== 2. Restore (infra/scripts/restore.sh, make restore FILE=…) ==
OP -> BE : stop backend
OP -> PG : pg_restore --clean FILE
OP -> REC : restore the recordings archive
OP -> BE : start backend
note right of OP
  RUNBOOK «Восстановление»: one recorded manual walk;
  make backup-verify. No gate-side restore test (too slow).
end note

== 3. Purge guard and status (E29) ==
A -> BE : GET /api/v1/admin/backup-status
BE -> DIR : read last.json
BE --> A : {available, finished_at, status, …}
A -> BE : POST /api/v1/admin/recordings/purge {dry_run: false}
BE -> DIR : read last.json
alt last.json OK and newer than every row to purge
  BE -> REC : delete WAVs, write recording_purge_audit (as today)
  BE --> A : 200 PurgeRecordingsResult
else missing, failed or older
  BE --> A : 409 BACKUP_REQUIRED
end
note over BE
  listAdminAlerts: BACKUP_STALE when last.json is older than 26 h,
  BACKUP_FAILED when its status is not OK.
end note

@enduml
